/ pace"},{"surface":"நெடுந்தேர்","parts":[{"text":"நெடும்","lemma":"neṭum","gloss":"tall"},{"text":"தேர்","lemma":"tēr","gloss":"chariot"}],"gloss":"tall chariot"},{"surface":"வல்லரோடு","parts":[{"text":"வல்லர்","lemma":"vallar","gloss":"capable men"},{"text":"ஓடு","lemma":"ōṭu","gloss":"with"}],"gloss":"with skilled charioteers"},{"surface":"ஊரா","parts":[{"text":"ஊரா","lemma":"ūrā","gloss":"not driving"}],"gloss":"not driving"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வம்பணி","parts":[{"text":"வம்பு","lemma":"vampu","gloss":"new"},{"text":"அணி","lemma":"aṇi","gloss":"adorned"}],"gloss":"newly-adorned"},{"surface":"யானை","parts":[{"text":"யானை","lemma":"yāṉai","gloss":"elephant"}],"gloss":"elephant"},{"surface":"வேந்துதலை","parts":[{"text":"வேந்து","lemma":"vēntu","gloss":"king"},{"text":"தலை","lemma":"talai","gloss":"upon"}],"gloss":"king coming against them"},{"surface":"வரினும்","parts":[{"text":"வரினும்","lemma":"varu","gloss":"even if he comes"}],"gloss":"even if he comes"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"உண்பது","parts":[{"text":"உண்பது","lemma":"uṇ","gloss":"that which is eaten"}],"gloss":"what they eat"},{"surface":"மன்னும்","parts":[{"text":"மன்னும்","lemma":"maṉṉum","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"indeed"},{"surface":"அதுவே","parts":[{"text":"அதுவே","lemma":"atu","gloss":"that itself"}],"gloss":"is only that"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பரிசில்","parts":[{"text":"பரிசில்","lemma":"paricil","gloss":"gift"}],"gloss":"the prize"},{"surface":"மன்னும்","parts":[{"text":"மன்னும்","lemma":"maṉṉum","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"indeed"},{"surface":"குருசில்கொண்","parts":[{"text":"குருசில்கொண்","lemma":"குருசில்கொண்","gloss":"received by the chief"}],"gloss":"received by the chief","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"டதுவே","parts":[{"text":"டதுவே","lemma":"டதுவே","gloss":"is only that"}],"gloss":"is only that","split_unverified":true}]}],"literal":"Big drops of rain fallen in water, / like bubbles, having round-pupiled eyes, / black-naped, big-eared, small hares / leap and frolic in the small bushes of the inner village. / If you go to that spacious common ground, / even if it is a distressed state where they cannot say \"eat!\", / O poets, stay and then go! It is very good. / Because of your going there, the wife, gladly, / since all the varagu and tinai millets that were there / were completely exhausted by needy people taking them to eat, / and because she could not obtain any loan to be repaid later, / she put the dried seed-millet into the mouth of the mortar, / and did she not bring out a little? She did not fail to do so! In her village, / in every house of the hunting clan, the granary ... / ... monitor lizard ... / Not driving long chariots with skilled charioteers, / even if the king with newly-adorned elephants comes against them, / what they eat is indeed only that, / and what the chief receives as a prize is indeed only that!","translation":"In the inner village, small hares with black napes, large ears, and round eyes like bubbles formed by heavy raindrops falling on water, leap and frolic in the small bushes. If you go to the spacious common ground of that village, O poets, stay there before you go; it will be very good. For when you arrive, the lady of the house will gladly welcome you. Since all the varagu and tinai millets they had were exhausted by needy guests, and she could not obtain any grain on loan from others, she did not hesitate to take the dried seed-millet saved for sowing, pound it in the mortar, and cook it for you. In that village of hunters, even if a mighty king with newly-adorned elephants comes to wage war, they do not ride in long chariots driven by skilled men; what they eat is only that simple millet, and the prize their chief wins is only the glory of battle!","modern":"நீரில் விழும் மழையின் பெரிய துளிகள் போன்ற குமிழிகள் போன்ற உருண்டையான விழிகளைக் கொண்ட, கரிய பிடரியும் பெரிய காதுகளும் உடைய சிறிய முயல்கள், ஊரின் உள்ளே இருக்கும் சிறிய புதர்களில் துள்ளி விளையாடுகின்றன. அத்தகைய வெட்டவெளியான மன்றத்திற்கு நீங்கள் சென்றால், வறுமையின் காரணமாக \"உண்ணுங்கள்\" என்று உபசரிக்க முடியாத துன்ப நிலை இருந்தாலும், புலவர்களே! நீங்கள் அங்கு தங்கிச் செல்லுங்கள்; அது மிகவும் நல்லது. நீங்கள் அங்கு சென்றவுடன், இல்லத்தரசி மகிழ்ச்சியடைந்து, வீட்டில் இருந்த வரகும் தினையும் இரப்பவர்கள் உண்டு தீர்த்துவிட்டதாலும், கைமாற்றாக வேறு யாரிடமும் கடன் பெற முடியாததாலும், விதைப்பதற்காக உலர வைத்து வைத்திருந்த விதைத்தினையை உரலில் இட்டுக் குத்தி, உங்களுக்குச் சமைத்துப் படைக்கத் தயங்க மாட்டாள். அவளுடைய ஊரில் உள்ள வேட்டுவக் குடிகள் தோறும்... உடும்பு... பாகர்களோடு நீண்ட தேர்களை ஓட்டி வராத, புதிய அணிகலன்களை அணிந்த யானைகளைக் கொண்ட வேந்தனே எதிர்த்து வந்தாலும், அவர்கள் உண்பது அந்த எளிய தினையையே; அந்தத் தலைவன் பெறும் பரிசும் போர்க்களத்து வெற்றியே ஆகும்.","explanation":"This poem belongs to the Vākai tiṇai and the Mūtiṉ Mullai tuṟai, which celebrates the ancient, noble, and brave house of a warrior. The speaker is a poet directing other visiting poets to the home of a generous but impoverished warrior. The poem opens with a vivid description of the village, where small hares with bubble-like eyes play in the bushes, establishing the rustic landscape. The core of the poem highlights the extraordinary hospitality of the warrior's wife, who, having no food left and unable to borrow any, does not hesitate to pound the precious seed-millet reserved for the next sowing to feed her guests. The concluding lines emphasize the warrior's fierce pride and simple life; even when threatened by a powerful king with elephants, the clan remains content with their simple food and values honor above all else.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}